      "worked_solution": "To multiply a complex number by a purely imaginary number, we use the distributive property and the fact that ${\\text{i}}^{2}=-1.$\n\nFor the given problem, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(7+12\\,\\text{i})\\cdot 5\\,\\text{i} & =7\\cdot 5\\,\\text{i}+12\\,\\text{i}\\cdot 5\\,\\text{i} \\\\  & =(7\\cdot 5)\\,\\text{i}+12\\cdot 5\\cdot {\\text{i}}^{2} \\\\  & =35\\,\\text{i}+60\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =35\\,\\text{i}-60 \\\\  & =-60+35\\,\\text{i}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
